        "original_id": "b9a94102-1d0d-5077-ae7a-a17ed142444b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Munich\n- Events: 1974 FIFA World Cup Final, 1974 FIFA World Cup\n- Organizations: West Germany national football team, Netherlands national football team\n- People: Jack Taylor\n- Topics: Football in Munich\n\nFacts:\n- Munich is described as one of the most successful footballing cities in Europe and the world, with over 40 trophies, including Germany's victory in the 1974 FIFA World Cup Final.\n- The 1974 FIFA World Cup Final was the final match of the 10th FIFA World Cup, which determined the world champion among national men's football teams.\n- The 1974 FIFA World Cup Final was contested by the Netherlands and West Germany, and West Germany won the match 2–1.\n- Jack Taylor, born on 21 April 1930 and died on 27 July 2012, was an English football referee known for officiating the 1974 FIFA World Cup Final and awarding two penalties in the first 30 minutes.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
